# Generated by Phase: IMPLEMENT | Feature: EVOL-080
"""Deliverable homes (EVOL-080): one source of truth per deliverable category.

categories  `CATEGORIES`, a closed list. `asked` categories (business, design, report) may live in an external store;
            every other category is derived to the repo, with its reason (the code compiles, runs or machine-reads it,
            or delivery state moves its bytes without an approval).
pin         `<artefact>.pin.json` = {source, id, version, approved_at, sha256} — the artefact in the tree. A file at the
            path wins over its pin (the draft of a refine); neither is an absent artefact.
reader      `text(repo, rel, ref=None)` — the one read every gate and agent makes. A pinned artefact is read live at the
            pinned version, never the latest: the current version in one call, the historical one only after drift;
            the version number and the sha256 must match the pin, else red. A run-scoped memo (`GATE_DOCUMENTS_MEMO`,
            set by `profile --run`) serves only bytes whose hash is the pin's.
writer      `approve` publishes at approval (a new version only when the bytes differ), writes the pin, removes the file;
            `pull` writes the pinned bytes back as the draft of a refine. Nothing else writes the store.
faults      `StoreDown` — the store could not answer (transport, 5xx, repeated 429, 401/403, no credential): `profile`
            reports the member n/a with a WARN; a direct call exits 2. Red, never infra: a missing page or version, a
            version or hash mismatch, a page that no longer carries one artefact block.
stores      `confluence` (Cloud v2 on *.atlassian.net, Data Center v1 elsewhere; the artefact is one code macro whose
            CDATA is the bytes) · `built` — commands built at materialisation, no shell: `read {id} {version}` prints
            {version, body}, `publish {id} {title} {file}` prints {id, version}; proven by `--probe`.
"""
